{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hominine-immaterial-armyworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Data Center refuses to null a sub-task's `fields.parent` (HTTP 400)\n\n## Provenance\n\nFiled to satisfy [rebar:88d9-fe42-e50f-4067]'s AC11, which pre-authorised this exact outcome:\n\n> UNLESS it reports its explicit `SETUP FAILED` message, which means Data Center refused to null a\n> sub-task's `fields.parent`. That is a PLATFORM finding, not this fix failing; record it and file\n> it separately rather than weakening the cell.\n\nObserved on harness run **30834117797** (job 91755000385, main @ `25ead49f3e`).\n\n## Evidence — verbatim\n\n> SETUP FAILED (not a rebar defect): Data Center REFUSED to clear the parent of sub-task RBJYRMS-2 —\n> BackendHTTPError: HTTP Error 400: JiraError HTTP 400 url:\n> http://localhost:2990/jira/rest/api/2/issue/10029\n\nThe message came from `test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips`'s SETUP, not its assertion: the cell\ncould not get Data Center into the precondition state it needed, so it never exercised the code\nunder test. The cell was deliberately built to report this case DISTINCTLY rather than as an\nambiguous red, and it did.\n\n## What this does and does not establish\n\n**Does:** DC 8.17.1 rejects a `PUT` that nulls a sub-task's `fields.parent`. A sub-task on DC must\nhave a parent — the field is structurally required — so there is no \"detached sub-task\" state for\nthe fixture to create.\n\n**Does not:** say anything about whether rebar's inbound parent clear works. That path's evidence is\nthe discriminating trio recorded on 88d9 (measured RED against both wrong states, GREEN against the\nfix) plus the full 2079-passing suite. The live cell simply cannot reach it on a sub-task.\n\n## Consequence — the inbound clear has no live coverage on DC\n\nThis is the honest statement of the gap, and it should not be papered over: the ONLY live cell for\nthe inbound parent clear is blocked by a platform constraint, so on Data Center that path is\nproven by unit evidence alone. Given that this epic has twice shipped mutation-proven code that was\nwrong in production (1276, 1288), unit-only coverage of a data-affecting path is a real risk, not a\nformality.\n\n## Options for restoring live coverage, none yet chosen\n\n 1. Use a NON-sub-task child whose parent is an Epic Link, and clear the epic link instead — a\n    different write path (greenhopper sentinel epic `\"none\"`), so it tests the clear the production\n    code would actually take for a non-sub-task.\n 2. Assert the refusal itself as the contract: pin that DC rejects the null so a future DC version\n    that starts accepting it fails loudly and tells us the coverage gap can be closed.\n 3. Accept unit-only coverage for the sub-task clear and record it as a known limit.\n\nOption 1 is the only one that yields real coverage, and it is closest to what a rebar deployment\nwould actually do, since [rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda] casts doubt on the sub-task write path working\nat all on this version.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] the refusal is confirmed against the target DC version with the raw response body recorded\n      (the current evidence is the status code and URL only)\n- [ ] one of the three options above is chosen, with the rejected ones and the reason recorded\n- [ ] if option 1 or 2: the cell lands and is GREEN on a live harness run, with the run id recorded\n- [ ] if option 3: the limitation is documented where a DC operator will see it, not only on a ticket","id":"37e7-d751-0042-4b94","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Data Center refuses to null a sub-task's fields.parent (HTTP 400): the inbound-clear live cell cannot reach its precondition"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785779901196705001,"uuid":"55252479-df57-4f5e-9439-c61b1bbd55d3"}